{"type":"lesson.started","request_id":"ddc8ea81-c9e6-4065-b46b-4837bbcebbc6","title":"Absolute value as distance on a number line"}
{"type":"lesson.step","request_id":"ddc8ea81-c9e6-4065-b46b-4837bbcebbc6","step":{"id":"s1","script":"Absolute value tells us a number’s distance from zero. Zero is already at zero, so its distance is zero.","ops":[{"op":"figure","id":"numberline","region":"left","frame":{"x":[-5.5,5.5],"y":[-1.2,1.8],"axes":"none"},"marks":[{"kind":"segment","id":"line","from":[-5,0],"to":[5,0],"arrow":true},{"kind":"point","id":"zero","at":[0,0],"label":"0"},{"kind":"point","id":"negative","at":[-4,0],"label":"−4"},{"kind":"point","id":"positive","at":[4,0],"label":"4"}]},{"op":"text","id":"title","region":"C1","content":"Absolute value = distance from zero"},{"op":"equation","id":"atzero","anchor":{"el":"title","side":"below","gap":0.08},"latex":"|0|=0"}],"checkpoint":null}}
{"type":"lesson.step","request_id":"ddc8ea81-c9e6-4065-b46b-4837bbcebbc6","step":{"id":"s2","script":"Four is four units to the right of zero. The bars ask for distance, so the absolute value of four is four.","ops":[{"op":"figure","id":"rightdistance","on":"numberline","marks":[{"kind":"segment","from":{"at":"positive"},"to":[4,0.8],"stroke":"dashed"},{"kind":"segment","from":{"at":"zero"},"to":[0,0.8],"stroke":"dashed"},{"kind":"measure","from":[0,0.8],"to":[4,0.8],"label":"4 units"}]},{"op":"equation","id":"positiveabs","anchor":{"el":"atzero","side":"below","gap":0.08},"latex":"|4|=4"}],"checkpoint":null}}
{"type":"lesson.step","request_id":"ddc8ea81-c9e6-4065-b46b-4837bbcebbc6","step":{"id":"s3","script":"Negative four is also four units from zero. Direction changes, but distance stays positive. Opposite numbers have the same absolute value.","ops":[{"op":"figure","id":"leftdistance","on":"numberline","marks":[{"kind":"segment","from":{"at":"negative"},"to":[-4,0.8],"stroke":"dashed"},{"kind":"measure","from":[-4,0.8],"to":[0,0.8],"label":"4 units"}]},{"op":"equation","id":"negativeabs","anchor":{"el":"positiveabs","side":"below","gap":0.08},"latex":"|-4|=4"},{"op":"text","id":"conclusion","anchor":{"el":"negativeabs","side":"below","gap":0.08},"content":"Distance is never negative."}],"checkpoint":{"question":"What is |−3|, and why?","expected_gist":"3, because −3 is three units from zero."}}}
